s find out about a traditional holiday!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment. ", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "John in Mexico", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Traditional Holidays", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Taking a Break > Baja", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Be Going To vs. The Present Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The structure<span class = \"italic\"> be going to + verb</span> and the Present Continuous tense are similar. They can be used to talk about the future.<br/><br/>You use the structure<span class=\"italic\"> be going to + verb</span> to talk about future intentions or decisions in a general way.<br/><br/>You use the Present Continuous tense for future plans or arrangements that have been planned or booked.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I'm staying in New York for two weeks.  (Present Continuous)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm going to stay in New York for a while. (Going to)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We're visiting Baja, California until November 5th. (Present Continuous)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We're going to visit Baja, California sometime next year. (Going to)", "type": "example"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le12ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Thanksgiving", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a traditional North American celebration of the harvest in autumn, in which people demonstrate how thankful they are for what they have", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are you going to be in New York for Thanksgiving?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le12ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about traditional holidays.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the second longest running ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "it has been going on for the most amount of time (except for one other), compared to other things like it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Macy's Parade is the second longest running Thanksgiving parade in the United States.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le12ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "marching band ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a musical group that plays instruments as they walk in a parade", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's famous for its colorful floats and marching bands. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le12ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "balloon", "type": "name"}, {"content": "thin plastic that becomes large when inflated with air or helium", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Macy's Parade has many balloons.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le12ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Santa Claus ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a historical figure who is said to bring gifts to children on Christmas Day", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Santa Claus makes an appearance at Herald Square at the end of the parade. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le12ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "festivity", "type": "name"}, {"content": "public events organized for a special occasion ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Make sure you check out the festivities for the Day of the Dead. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le12ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose a country you don't know much about. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go online. Find a traditional holiday from that country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Complete the table with information you found.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present the holiday to your classmates.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I choose a country to learn about.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I find information about a traditional holiday.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I complete the table about holidays.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present the information.", "type": "text"}]}]}